  "body": "## What happens\n\n`cargo xtask gate batch` fails on main since `ea19c3f21` (merge of PR #3942). The step \"debug build: app (--no-run)\" stops with:\n\n    error[E0560]: struct `camcraft_app::operation::WireContourOp` has no field named `start`\n      --> crates/app/tests/wire_dxf_selection/arcs.rs:49:9\n      --> crates/app/tests/wire_dxf_selection/arcs.rs:135:35\n\nThe post-merge runs of `099895715` (dude) and `98caf2dfd` (wopr-2) are red for this reason. The runs on HotTamale and FlamingFire_System are red for runner setup reasons (#3947).\n\n## Cause\n\nThe two PRs merged cleanly in git but disagree:\n\n- PR #3871 (#3339) moved the wire start point from `WireContourOp::start` into `picks: PathPicks`.\n- PR #3942 (#3937), merged after it, added `wire_dxf_selection/arcs.rs`, which still sets `start`.\n\nOnly test code is affected. The product code compiles.\n\n## Done means\n\n`arcs.rs` sets the start pick through `picks` (the same form #3871 used in the other wire tests), `wire_dxf_selection` compiles and passes, and the batch gate on main builds the app tests again.\n",
